parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2-ternary

Model weights and model card (export.safetensors, manifest.json,
reconstruction.json, tokenizer/, README.md): CC-BY-4.0, see LICENSE.
Software (load_ternary.py): MIT License, copyright and permission notice at the
top of that file.

This model is a modified version of nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2
(https://huggingface.co/nvidia/parakeet-tdt-0.6b-v2, revision
ae9ad07059c7c739ffaf932226a8fe64ae2620b0), (c) NVIDIA, licensed CC-BY-4.0
(https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/). The modified model is
distributed under the same license; see LICENSE. No endorsement by NVIDIA is
implied.

Changes made to the original model:
- In each of the 24 encoder layers, the feed-forward projections
  (feed_forward1/2.linear1/2), the self-attention projections
  (linear_q, linear_k, linear_v, linear_out, linear_pos) and the pointwise
  convolutions (conv.pointwise_conv1/2) were retrained with quantization-aware
  training, distilling from the original model, and are stored as ternary codes
  {-1, 0, +1} (2 bits, four per byte) with one FP32 scale per output row
  (264 matrices, 603,979,776 parameters).
- All other tensors (subsampling front end, depthwise convolutions, norms,
  biases, the prediction and joint networks, which were not trained) are stored
  in FP16, except the feature-extraction window and mel filterbank (FP32) and
  integer BatchNorm counters.
- The weights are distributed as safetensors with a manifest and a standalone
  loader (load_ternary.py) instead of a .nemo archive. The tokenizer files and
  the model configuration are unchanged copies from the original .nemo archive.

Training data (audio only; training targets were transcripts generated by the
original model, human transcripts were used only for filtering):
- YODAS-Granary, English
  (https://huggingface.co/datasets/espnet/yodas-granary, revision
  969944574ea3f37890beaf67ea651e160cfaf043), CC-BY-3.0. References:
  "Yodas: Youtube-oriented dataset for audio and speech",
  https://arxiv.org/abs/2406.00899; "Granary: Speech Recognition and
  Translation Dataset in 25 European Languages",
  https://arxiv.org/pdf/2505.13404.
- LibriSpeech train.clean.100, train.clean.360 and train.other.500
  (https://huggingface.co/datasets/openslr/librispeech_asr, revision
  71cacbfb7e2354c4226d01e70d77d5fca3d04ba1), CC-BY-4.0.
- People's Speech, clean configuration
  (https://huggingface.co/datasets/MLCommons/peoples_speech, revision
  f10597c5d3d3a63f8b6827701297c3afdf178272). The clean configuration selects
  CC-BY material; the CC-BY version (2.0, 2.5, 3.0 or 4.0) depends on the
  source recording.
- VoxPopuli, English train (https://huggingface.co/datasets/facebook/voxpopuli,
  revision 42f01879c780b4a2e90ec0b4f616c2ece526e4f1), CC0-1.0.
- AMI, IHM train (https://huggingface.co/datasets/edinburghcstr/ami, revision
  46f28f2503e2ec48f8867a84eef356c70476beab), CC-BY-4.0; publisher license
  statement: https://groups.inf.ed.ac.uk/ami/corpus/.

